he month value is between 1 and 12.\"\"\"\n    return _MIN_MONTH <= month <= _MAX_MONTH\ndef _check_day(day: int, month: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates the day based on the month's specific day range.\"\"\"\n    if not (_MIN_DAY <= day):\n        return False\n    if month in _MONTHS_31_DAYS:\n        return day <= _MAX_DAY_31\n    elif month in _MONTHS_30_DAYS:\n        return day <= _MAX_DAY_30\n    elif month == _FEBRUARY_MONTH:\n        return day <= _MAX_DAY_29\n    return False # Should not be reached if _check_month passed\ndef valid_date(date: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates a given date string according to specific format and business rules.\n    Returns True if the date is valid, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if not date:\n        return False\n\n    if not _check_format(date):\n        return False\n\n    try:\n        month, day, year = _parse_date(date)\n    except ValueError: # Catch potential errors from int() conversion if format check was insufficient\n        return False\n\n    if not _check_month(month):\n        return False\n\n    if not _check_day(day, month):\n        return False\n\n    return True", "base_status": "pass", "plus_status": "fail", "base_fail_tests": [], "plus_fail_tests": [["06-04-2020\n"]]}], "HumanEval/125": [{"task_id": "HumanEval/125", "solution": "def _is_odd_position(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a character is a lowercase letter at an odd alphabetical position.\n    Zero-based alphabetical ordering (a=0, b=1, ..., z=25) is used.\n    \"\"\"\n    if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n        position = ord(char) - ord('a')\n        return position % 2 != 0\n    return False\ndef _count_odd_lowercase_letters(txt: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts lowercase letters with odd alphabetical positions in the input string.\n    It iterates through the string and uses _is_odd_position for each character.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for char in txt:\n        if _is_odd_position(char):\n            count += 1\n  